Vendored, patched copy of iced_tiny_skia
----------------------------------------

`vendor/iced_tiny_skia/` is iced_tiny_skia 0.14.1, MIT licensed, copyright
2019 Héctor Ramón Jiménez and the iced contributors
(https://github.com/iced-rs/iced). It is vendored unmodified except for one
patch, marked with an "AuraPass patch" comment in
`src/window/compositor.rs`:

  `present()` now always damages the whole window instead of asking iced to
  diff consecutive frames. The automatic diff groups damage rectangles in a
  single pass, so overlapping translucent layers — anti-aliased text, card
  shadows, the modal scrim — were composited more than once per frame and
  drifted towards black, and areas that stopped being drawn kept stale pixels.
  A full-frame present is the same path the screenshot renderer already used,
  costs little for a flat interface at this size, and is deterministic.

The patch is AuraPass's own work and is offered under the same MIT OR
Apache-2.0 terms as the rest of AuraPass. Send upstream fixes to the iced
project; they are not AuraPass changes.

Vendored, patched copy of iced_widget
-------------------------------------

`vendor/iced_widget/` is iced_widget 0.14.2, MIT licensed, copyright 2019
Héctor Ramón Jiménez and the iced contributors
(https://github.com/iced-rs/iced). It is vendored with two small patches,
marked with "AuraPass patch" comments in `src/scrollable.rs` (and an import
cleanup in `src/pick_list.rs`):

  `scrollable.rs` now gives the scrollbar thumb a 36 px minimum length and
  clamps its travel inside the track. The stock renderer computes a
  proportional thumb with a 2 px floor, which is nearly impossible to grab in a
  1,600-item list.

  `pick_list.rs` drops a legacy `use std::f32;` import so the crate builds
  without a deprecated-constant warning on the current toolchain.

These patches are AuraPass's own work and are offered under the same MIT OR
Apache-2.0 terms as the rest of AuraPass. Send upstream fixes to the iced
project; they are not AuraPass changes.

Data files
----------

  * `crates/aurapass-core/data/eff_large_wordlist.txt` is the Electronic
    Frontier Foundation's "long word list", published in 2016 for passphrase
    generation and distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
    United States license.
    https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2016/07/new-wordlists-random-passphrases
    The file is used unchanged; the 7,776 words and their dice numbers are the
    EFF's.

Specifications implemented
--------------------------

  * RFC 8439 — ChaCha20 and Poly1305 for IETF Protocols.
  * draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03 — XChaCha20 and XChaCha20-Poly1305.
  * RFC 5869 — HMAC-based Extract-and-Expand Key Derivation Function (HKDF).
  * RFC 6238 — TOTP: Time-Based One-Time Password Algorithm.
  * RFC 4226 — HOTP: An HMAC-Based One-Time Password Algorithm.
  * RFC 4648 — The Base16, Base32, and Base64 Data Encodings.
  * Argon2 (RFC 9106) via the `argon2` crate.
  * Debian Policy Manual and the Filesystem Hierarchy Standard.

Format interoperability
-----------------------

  * The Enpass JSON, 1Password 1PIF/CSV, Bitwarden JSON, LastPass CSV and
    KeePass CSV/Xml importers were written against vendor-published export
    formats and, for 1PIF, against the format as documented by 1Password.
  * Have I Been Pwned range queries use the k-anonymity API v3 documented at
    https://haveibeenpwned.com/API/v3#PwnedPasswords.

